{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-252598",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n${log}_{b}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={b}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare ${log}_{25}⁡5=\\frac{1}{2}$ with ${log}_{b}⁡a=x,$ we get $a=5,$ $b=25,$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to ${25}^{1/2}=5,$ which is also equivalent to $\\sqrt{25}=5.$ Consequently, $b=25.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
